y-id "q-34725" :question/problem "$\\text{dim}(\\text{Span}{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]})=$" :question/worked-solution "We start by creating a matrix whose columns are made up of our vectors, and then we reduce the matrix to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns correspond to basis vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, the reduced matrix has $2$ pivot columns (or alternatively, it has exactly $2$ non-zero rows). \n\nTherefore, \n$\\text{dim}(\\text{Span}{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]})=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-34725/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "004c4177-ca0e-586c-962a-1220b4b64f47"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-34725"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-35299/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "262799ff-b132-5e55-9eda-a9ac31f13823" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35299/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "d1a576db-ad67-5df6-b441-cc40af5d3bda" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35299/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "2affd556-b83d-522e-ad98-2dd7fd57de31" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35299/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055cee